[Music]  [Applause]  over the course of 35 years and 20 plus  games we've seen a wide array of  recurring groups and characters zora  gorons rito koroks and more have all  been brought back at least once to play  a part in link's adventure once again  and yet at the same time there are also  those who've only been featured in one  game and are never seen again after that  say for some small references and  nothing more which brings us to the  minish also known as the picori to the  hylians though fun fact this is actually  unique to the english version of minish  cap alone yes for the other language  versions including japanese this  distinction doesn't exist and both  hylians and minish use the same name i  have no idea why they decided to change  this for the english version but let's  just say it wouldn't be the first time  that nintendo of america altered emitted  or inserted their own ideas into a zelda  game diminish are one of my personal  favorite creatures in the entire series  tiny thumb-sized beings who resemble  anthropomorphic mice and made their  debut in 2004's the legend of zelda  minish cap they remind me a lot of the  borrowers from arietti which as of right  now is in my top 5 miyazaki films  however unlike the borrowers the minish  are completely invisible to most people  in that regard they have a lot more in  common with the koroks who are also said  to be invisible except to those who are  pure of heart particularly children but  a big difference between the koroks and  the minish is that their origin is not  found inside the kingdom of hyrule but  rather a mysterious dimension called the  minish realm they even have their own  highly complex language  funnily enough they are perhaps most  famous for being the ones responsible as  to why link keeps finding rupees and  other trinkets hidden inside grass and  empty jars as it's said to be their way  of offering gifts and good fortune to  the hylians something that before this  game was just a funny unexplained staple  of the zelda series but their influence  on hyrule cannot be underestimated and  goes far beyond just leaving behind  small collectibles despite their size  they've had a huge impact on the outcome  of events in the battle between good and  evil mostly for the better but in one  particular case for the worst being one  of my favorite zelda creatures i had  honestly given up all hope that we would  ever see them again nintendo has had  plenty of opportunities to bring them  back as there are no less than 7 games  which were released after diminished cap  you can also imagine my disappointment  when i found out that nintendo did  actually have plans to include a race of  tiny beings in the latest zelda epic  breath of the wild but was ultimately  scrapped to meet the deadline link would  have had the ability to shrink down to  their size and interact with them  similar to the 2004 game boy advance  title something which probably required  too much additional programming to get  it done in time remember breath of the  wild was already delayed like four times  now it only exists as yet another idea  of what could have been hidden away in  developer notes and a single screenshot  but then something happened which at the  time wasn't something most people were  expecting a direct sequel to breath of  the wild was announced one of only a few  direct sequels in the zelda timeline not  only that but it stars the same main  characters and takes place in the same  world no less which is actually a first  for the series so knowing what we know  now are there any hints or at least  possible story implications that would  warrant the return of hyrule's tiniest  heroes well yes and surprisingly more  than you would think the first and most  obvious one of course being the fact  that as stated before there were  minish-like beings conceptualized for  breath of the wild and nintendo is  definitely no stranger to taking  discarded ideas and carrying them over  to the next installment but that kind of  speaks for itself and on its own it's  not exactly convincing evidence as there  are many many ideas which didn't make it  into breath the wild and i highly doubt  we'll see all of them implemented in the  sequel so what else is there well let's  start with trivia story and lore  connections  although taking place in the same  overworld as its predecessor breath of  the wild 2 has been revealed to take  place at least partially in the skies  above hyrule as of yet we still don't  know what exactly this place is but many  are speculating that this isn't just  high above hyrule but perhaps a  different realm altogether reason being  is that in breath of the wild as well as  the footage from the sequel trailer  where link is on the surface the sky  islands are nowhere to be seen but how  does this relate to diminish well the  minis realm is said to reside in the  heavens or at least close to it this is  depicted as such in hyrule historia but  it's also told to us in the backstory to  minish cap sometime between skyward  sword and minish cap when hyrule was  being plagued by evil diminish appeared  from the heavens gifting the hylians a  sword known as the picori blade and a  golden light which is implied to be the  triforce i guess or at least part of it  but we'll cover that in a different  video over the course of minish cap's  adventure this legendary blade is first  broken then reforged by diminish and  subsequently infused with four elements  by link himself and henceforth became  known as the four sword thereafter  canonically this is the same blade  featured in four swords and four swords  adventures the existence of the four  sword is not irrelevant when it comes to  the possible story of breftwat 2 believe  it or not and this has everything to do  with the return of everyone's favorite  pigman ganondorf as of today it's still  not confirmed which timeline breath of  the wild follows up on but ganondorf  being back in his human form rather than  his alter-ego ganon has led to many  people leaning more and more towards the  child timeline i'm not going to get too  deep into why as that is a video on its  own and i'm not even making the claim  that the child timeline is without a  doubt where breath of the wild belongs  but it has mostly to do with the fact  that the corpse we see in the breathtak  2 teaser has similar characteristics of  that of ganondorf from twilight princess  as well as the fact that this is the  only timeline where we visually saw the  demon king transforming into malice  something that is referred to in  creating a champion here's the problem  though according to the official zelda  timeline twilight princess isn't the  last game in the child branch to feature  ganondorf but instead four swords  adventures here ganondorf has been  reincarnated into his human gerudo form  transforms into ganon and is last seen  being sealed inside the four sword so if  nintendo wants to keep at least some  story consistency and breath of the wild  in its sequel take place in the child  timeline technically ganon should be  inside the four sword unless he broke  free from it somewhere between four  swords adventures and breath of the wild  which is possible but then what happened  to the four sword and where is it now of  course it could be that nintendo decides  to totally ignore this part of zelda's  history heck many people even doubt if  four swords adventure's timeline  placement is accurate and should perhaps  be placed somewhere else but unless  nintendo ever updates the timeline it  remains where it is now at the end of  the child branch next is visual hints  from the recent e3 trailer for the  sequel first off we have a shield which  link is seen carrying that has a symbol  on it that is eerily similar to that of  vati the main antagonist from minish cap  if this symbol turns out to be more than  just a little reference this could be  huge in terms of a possible return of  diminish not only was vati the main  antagonist in the game which first  introduced diminish but he is one  himself or at least he was before  transforming into a demon vati is also  the only main zelda antagonist to have  directly interacted with ganon sure  ganon has interacted with other villains  before like xand twin rover general onox  and varan but these all turned out to be  side villains in their own respective  games and in service of ganon vati is  the only one who played the role of main  antagonist devoid of ganon's presence  only to meet him in a later game he's a  lot more ancient than ganon preceding  him by many millennia and is actually  the first prominent demon to make an  appearance in hyrule after demise's  curse is uttered in skyward sword vati  also has a close connection to the four  sword as he's been sealed inside it no  less than two times obviously i'm not  saying that vati will be present in  breath dwelt too but the fact that we  find a possible reference to him does  make a return of diminish more probable  after all who made this shield and how  does anybody even remember vati after  all this time another possible  connection to diminish are the green  robot creatures seen in the second  teaser it's not like we haven't seen  robots before in breath the wild but  it's obvious that the ones seen here are  very different from the shika made  guardians the minish cap details that  diminish have created automata in the  past the game features these robotic  soldiers and one of the minish in this  area explains that they themselves built  these machines to help the humans in  their fight against evil these  mechanical soldiers are also almost  exclusively found inside the wind ruins  which have a connection to a tribe that  used to live here and have since built  their new home in the sky and now here  we find robots who reside in the sky  there's also something else i want to  mention and i do realize that this is  definitely a stretch but remember those  weird reversed vocals we hear in the two  teasers well in the japanese german and  italian versions of minish cap diminish  actually speak in reverse and although  not canon this trait was even carried  over to the english version of diminish  cap manga again a huge stretch i know  but i still felt like it was at least  worth mentioning the next exhibit is not  in the form of story or visual elements  but in the form of a man hidemaru  fujibayashi director of breath of the  wild skyward sword and minish cap as  well as the guy behind the stories of  oracle of ages and seasons when he was  still working at capcom it's clear from  fujibashi's track record that he likes  to tell stories and in particular origin  stories the man himself has on camera no  less expressed regret that the idea of  minish-like creatures in breath of the  wild did not make it in it even shows  footage of diminished cap as  [Music]  like  [Music]  [Music]  since he'll be returning as director for  the upcoming sequel as well there is a  chance that he will go out of his way to  secure their inclusion this time around  and since the sequel will reuse the same  engine there will be a lot more time to  make it happen fujibarashi is the one  who came up with vati the four sword and  diminish so i'd imagine he would be  delighted to incorporate more of the  lore he created into the game especially  considering that breath of the wild was  already packed with references to  skyward sword most of which he created  as well at least story wise this leaves  us with one final question if diminish  would make a comeback in breathtak 2 how  exactly would that work in terms of  gameplay and what kind of connection  could they have to the main story in  minish cap link could shrink in size due  to eslo a cursed minish who possesses  powerful magic he is seen casting runes  around link after which he shrinks down  to minish size however the game never  states that this is the only way to  achieve this in fact it specifically  says that the hylians and minish used to  have a much closer connection and even  met with each other regularly not only  that but apparently even adults were  able to see them back then but over time  the two races grew apart for unknown  reasons it's clear that eslo's magic  power is not unique in this regard the  ancient highlands had magic of their own  which allowed them to speak to diminish  at the deepwood shrine which is said to  have served as sort of a meeting point  for the two races and perhaps in breath  of the wild too the magical abilities  link receives from his afflicted arm  could allow him to shrink as well and as  a final stray thought is it me or does  link's appearance in the breath wall 2  trailer look a bit similar to the  ancient hylian hero of men especially  the hairstyle but i don't know i'm  probably making connections that aren't  there anyway there is a lot more to talk  about when it comes to diminish but i'll  save that for a follow-up video where i  will talk more about the golden light  and some other ideas i have about this  era i think the idea of becoming small  could really work for breath the world  too it was already a joy to see hyrule  from a different perspective in minish  gap the way normal everyday objects  suddenly serve as tools obstacles or  even houses now imagine that but in full  3d it would also be yet another way to  make breath the wild's hyrule feel brand  new again despite the fact that we've  already explored this world even if the  minish don't show up i at least hope  that there will be some references to  them as there weren't that many in  breath the wild but the minish are a  crucial part of hyrule's history in my  opinion they forged a powerful sword one  of a few besides the master sword  capable of defeating ganon they bestowed  powerful magic upon the hylians in their  time of need and as far as races go they  might just be the one who reside closest  to the gods  [Music]  before ending the video i want to give a  shout out to bannon who gifted me an  amazing homemade minish figurine as well  as an awesome oil painting of breath to  waltz hyrule i cannot express enough how  thankful i am for this and well humbled  that you would want to give me such an  amazing piece of artwork which i'm  guessing took quite a while to make if  you're interested in one of these  figurines or other types of zelda art  yourself there's a link to their twitter  and facebook in the description if you  want to check it out not a sponsorship  by the way just a way to help a fellow  artist who's been so generous with me so  again a big thanks to bannon rest  assured that this little guy will be  sitting comfortably on my shelf for many  many years to come additionally a big  thanks to all of you for watching to my  mods my patreons and members who  continue to make my content possible and  to clifford longhead jr alexander and  mika for joining the crew it is as  always much appreciated and that is all  for now this is don signing off and have  a good one  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  you

